BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Social Events
UID:event_317146491@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20261114T061848Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261115T130000
SUMMARY:English Spanish Language Conversation
DESCRIPTION:Language Exchange Toronto - Se Habla English & Spanish\n**Span
 ish Language Conversation Toronto** is part of ***Se Habla.***\n**“Se Ha
 bla”** is a leading online community for cultural and linguistic exchang
 e where you can participate in enriching sessions\, make new friends\, and
  connect with a growing global network. With 9 Meetup groups across 9 citi
 es in 6 countries\, Se Habla is truly open to everyone from Alaska to Pata
 gonia\, and from Europe and Asia to Australia. Join us and don’t miss th
 e opportunity to practice with native speakers.\n\n**We have been meeting 
 since June 2020 on the following days:**\n\n* Monday\n* Wednesday\n* Sunda
 y\n\nWith a one-time donation\, you can join the meetings as many times as
  you like and stay as long as you wish.\n\n**Format**\n**Conversation Room
 s (All levels)**\nDepending on attendance and nationality\, small groups a
 re formed with 4-6 people:\n\n* 2 native English speakers\n* 2 native Span
 ish speakers\n* 1 native speaker of another language\n\nThe meetings last 
 for 2 hours and are divided into 4 periods:\n\n* 30 minutes speaking in En
 glish\n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n* 30 minutes speaking in English\
 n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n\n**Beginner Room (Mondays and Wednesda
 y)**\nWelcome\, English and Spanish beginners.\n**Check the English and Sp
 anish lessons** here **»** [https://myspanishclass.xyz/](https://myspanis
 hclass.xyz/)\n\nPlease note that **we speak half of the time in English an
 d half in Spanish.** We help each other learn both languages.\n\n**After t
 wo hours**\, everyone returns to the main room to meet all participants an
 d take a group screenshot. If you have time\, you’re welcome to stay and
  continue the conversation for as long as you like.\n\n**Community**\n**We
  have 9 MeetUp groups meeting at the same time** (Mexico City\, Calgary\, 
 Vancouver\, Toronto\, New York\, London\, Los Angeles\, Medellín\, and Sa
 ntiago de Chile). However\, during the exchange\, you will meet people not
  only from these cities but also from all over the world.\n\nYou can get t
 he link to our 9 MeetUp groups by visiting any of the following pages:\n[h
 ttps://se-habla.com/spanish-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/spanish-meetup/)
 \n[[https://se-habla.com/english-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/english-mee
 tup/)\n\n**One-Time Donation**\nFor over four years\, the meetings were fr
 ee\, but currently I am requesting a **ONE-TIME DONATION** to access the m
 eetings and help to cover the costs of the 9 MeetUp Groups and Zoom.\n\nYo
 u can make the one-time donation at the link below. Afterward\, PayPal wil
 l redirect you to a page where you'll find the Zoom link to join the meeti
 ng.\n[https://se-habla.com/language-exchange](https://se-habla.com/languag
 e-exchange/)\n\nIf you have already donated and don't have the Zoom link\,
  please contact me.\n\n**Please don’t hesitate to reach out if you have 
 any further questions.**\n\nSee you soon\,\n**Héctor Fuentes**
