 for 2 hours and are divided into 4 periods:\n\n* 30 minutes speaking in En
 glish\n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n* 30 minutes speaking in English\
 n* 30 minutes speaking in Spanish\n\n**Beginner Room (Mondays and Wednesda
 ys)**\nWelcome\, English and Spanish beginners.\n**Check the English and S
 panish lessons** **here »** [https://myspanishclass.xyz/](https://myspani
 shclass.xyz/)\n\nPlease note that **we speak half of the time in English a
 nd half in Spanish.** We help each other learn both languages.\n\n**After 
 two hours**\, everyone returns to the main room to meet all participants a
 nd take a group screenshot. If you have time\, you’re welcome to stay an
 d continue the conversation for as long as you like.\n\n**Community**\n**W
 e have 9 MeetUp groups meeting at the same time** (Mexico City\, Calgary\,
  Vancouver\, Toronto\, New York\, London\, Los Angeles\, Medellín\, and S
 antiago de Chile). However\, during the exchange\, you will meet people no
 t only from these cities but also from all over the world.\n\nYou can get 
 the link to our 9 MeetUp groups by visiting any of the following pages:\n[
 https://se-habla.com/spanish-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/spanish-meetup/
 )\n[[https://se-habla.com/english-meetup/](https://se-habla.com/english-me
 etup/)\n\n**One-Time Donation**\nFor over four years\, the meetings were f
 ree\, but currently I am requesting a **ONE-TIME DONATION** to access the 
 meetings and help to cover the costs of the 9 MeetUp Groups and Zoom.\n\nY
 ou can make the one-time donation at the link below. Afterward\, PayPal wi
 ll redirect you to a page where you'll find the Zoom link to join the meet
 ing.\n[https://se-habla.com/language-exchange](https://se-habla.com/langua
 ge-exchange/)\n\nIf you have already donated and don't have the Zoom link\
 , please contact me.\n\n**Please don’t hesitate to reach out if you have
  any further questions.**\n\nSee you soon\,\nHéctor Fuentes
